{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From the [D]tribe of Zebulun [A]stood a [D]man
Gaddiel [G]son of Sodi [A]was his [D]name
Moses [G]sent him from [A]the Wilderness [Bm]of Paran
To [G]scout the land as the [A]Lord did com[D]mand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He walked through the Ne[A]gev up to He[D]bron
Saw [G]the giants [A]there, the strong and the [D]seven
They cut [G]a cluster in [A]the Valley [Bm]of Eshcol
[G]And carried it on [A]a pole for the [D]whole
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Forty [G]days they wandered [D]out
And came [Bm]back to show the [A]fruit
[G]The land flows with milk and honey
But [D]the people are [A/C#]too strong to [Bm]suit
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
They re[D]ported to the [A]congrega[D]tion
In Ka[G]desh by the wil[A]derness [D]land
[G]Caleb spoke to [A]quiet the [Bm]fear
But [G]others said [A]we cannot [D]stand
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
We seemed [G]like grasshoppers in their [D]eyes
De[Bm]voured by the land we [A]spied
The [G]congregation wept through the [D]night
[Bm]Grumbling loud [A]against their [D]guide
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[G]Back to Egypt they wished to go
[D]Leaving the prom[A/C#]ise to [Bm]break
{end_of_verse}

